        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "1b039398-31c1-52c9-bcee-b9d975ec9955",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Asgard\n- Concepts: Norse mythology\n- Organizations: Marvel Comics, Atlas Comics\n- Products: Journey into Mystery\n- People: Stan Lee, Larry Lieber, Jack Kirby, Thor\n- Topics: comic book publication history\n\nFacts:\n- Journey into Mystery is an American comic book series that was initially published by Atlas Comics and later by Marvel Comics.\n- In the late 1950s, Journey into Mystery changed from a horror comics anthology to giant-monster and science fiction stories.\n- Asgard first appeared in Journey into Mystery #83 in October 1962.\n- Stan Lee, Larry Lieber, and Jack Kirby created the first comics appearance of Asgard.\n- Asgard in Marvel Comics is based on the realm of the same name from Norse mythology.\n- Asgard is home to the Asgardians and other beings adapted from Norse mythology.\n- Asgard features prominently in stories about the Marvel Comics superhero Thor.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
